# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NO KEY IS NEEDED FOR THE HEADLINE RESULTS.
#
#   npm test                     295 tests
#   npm run verify:theorem       the theorem, from the shipped integrator
#   npm run verify:braid-2       every BRAID-2 number
#   npm run verify:reflex-silent TCAS is silent through the encounter
#   npm run verify:determinism   4 arms, byte-identical across runs
#   npm run ablate               3 arms x 200 seeds
#   npm run retrace:explore      200 schedules
#   npm run record:trace         regenerates fixtures/trace.json
#   npm run demo:live            replays the live run from the committed cache
#
# All of the above run with this file absent. The live runs below replay from
# fixtures/live-cache.jsonl with ZERO API calls; keys are only needed to RE-record.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The one endpoint this project actually uses. Both variables are required
# together — mimoFromEnv() returns null unless BOTH are set, and every
# participant then degrades to replaying the cache.
#
# Any Anthropic-protocol-compatible endpoint works; the committed cache was
# recorded against MiMo (mimo-v2.5-pro).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...
ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=...

# Leave unset. When set, mozaik's EventPublisherLoopVisitor ships every agent's
# full memory, tools and manifest to the cloud on every event, so runs stop
# being hermetic. See docs/API-NOTES.md #14.
# MOZAIK_API_KEY=...

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT USED, and said plainly rather than implied.
#
# An earlier design put each controller seat on a different vendor and gave the
# deceiving pilot its own OpenAI-compatible endpoint. That was abandoned: all
# three seats run on one model, MULTI_VENDOR is false, and a test asserts it.
# The deception result was dropped for the same reason — pilot and controller
# would share weights, so "a model chose to deceive and another caught it" would
# be self-play. The fuel discrepancy is injected into the sheet instead, so
# detection stays arithmetic and ground-truthed.
#
# OPENAI_API_KEY and GEMINI_API_KEY are read in exactly one place —
# configuredProviders() in model-roster.ts, which only reports what is
# configured. No participant consults them. Setting them changes nothing.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
